1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,080
Glaucoma is often called the silent thief of sight, and if you have not had a baseline eye exam since turning 40, it is worth checking now.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:13,840
Fluid inside your eye cannot drain properly, so pressure builds and presses on the optic nerve.

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:23,040
Unlike macular degeneration, which blurs central vision first, glaucoma creeps in from the edges, so most people do not notice until real damage is done.

4
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:29,920
Here is what surprises people: many with glaucoma test in the normal eye pressure range, called normal-tension glaucoma.

5
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:34,560
A pressure check alone can miss it, so ask for a visual field exam too.

6
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:43,440
Risk climbs after 40, with a family history, or if you are Black or Hispanic, since glaucoma is six to eight times more common in Black Americans.

7
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:49,440
That is why the American Academy of Ophthalmology recommends a baseline eye exam at 40 for everyone.

8
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:58,640
Head-down yoga poses like downward dog can spike eye pressure within a minute, while regular aerobic exercise like walking or swimming tends to lower it.

9
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:05,200
Sudden severe eye pain with headache and nausea, or rainbow-colored halos around lights, is an emergency.

10
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:09,520
Vision loss can happen within a day or two, so get to an eye doctor right away.

11
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:15,360
Glaucoma cannot undo damage already done, but catching it early protects the vision you still have.
